@startuml
' OWNER-MVP-2026-11-04 review: MVP core / cross-cutting. Core presentation/application/files or shared authority/recovery invariant remains applicable.
title Candidate resilience composition — not a generic retry-all wrapper
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

rectangle "Operation-specific eligibility / repetition policy" as P
rectangle "Bulkhead / admission budget\nBounded work class and shared headroom" as B
rectangle "Circuit breaker if justified\nScoped dependency health/admission" as C
rectangle "Adapter with evaluated deadline / timeout\nTimeout does not confirm remote stop" as A
rectangle "Actual outcome classification" as O
rectangle "Safe read / proven no-effect local failure\nBounded retry only when contract permits" as R
rectangle "Possible consequential effect\nSame-attempt reconciliation, no blind repeat" as U
P --> B
B --> C
C --> A : closed / eligible controlled probe
A --> O
O --> R : known safe eligibility
O --> U : partial / unknown effect
legend bottom
 Values, backend, isolation budget, breaker scope and probe mechanism require evaluation.
 Bulkheads reduce resource coupling, not security isolation. A timeout/breaker cannot prove no external effect.
 Backoff, jitter and attempt limits apply only after actual repetition safety is established.
endlegend
@enduml
